---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '../data/site';
---

<Layout title={`Privacy · ${siteConfig.name}`} description={`How ${siteConfig.name}'s website handles personal data.`}>
  <article class="legal">
    <a href="/" class="legal-back">‹ Home</a>
    <h1 class="legal-title">Privacy</h1>
    <p class="legal-updated">Last updated November 2026</p>

    <div class="prose">
      <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
      <p>
        This is the personal website of {siteConfig.name}, {siteConfig.location}. You can reach me through the
        contact form on this site or on <a href={siteConfig.socials.linkedin} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">LinkedIn</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>What is collected</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Contact form.</strong> If you send a message, I receive your name, email address, subject and message.</li>
        <li><strong>Server logs.</strong> The hosting provider (GitHub Pages) records standard technical data such as IP address, browser and time of request, for security and operations.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>There is no analytics, no advertising and no tracking cookies.</p>

      <h2>Why, and on what legal basis</h2>
      <p>
        Messages are processed to read and reply to your enquiry, on the basis of legitimate interest
        (Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR).
      </p>

      <h2>Browser storage</h2>
      <p>
        The site stores one value in your browser’s <code>localStorage</code>: <code>theme</code>, which
        remembers whether you chose light or dark mode. You can clear it at any time in your browser settings.
      </p>

      <h2>Third parties</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>GitHub Pages</strong> (GitHub, Inc.) hosts the site.</li>
        <li><strong>Formspree</strong> (Formspree, Inc.) delivers contact form messages to my inbox.</li>
        <li><strong>cdnjs</strong> (Cloudflare, Inc.) serves the icon font used on the site.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How long data is kept</h2>
      <p>
        Messages are kept only as long as needed for the conversation they belong to. They are never added to
        mailing lists or shared with others.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        Under the GDPR you can ask to access, correct or delete your personal data, or object to its processing.
        Send a request through the contact form or LinkedIn. You can also lodge a complaint with the Dutch Data
        Protection Authority (Autoriteit Persoonsgegevens).
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>

<style>
  .legal {
    max-width: 692px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 64px var(--gutter) 112px;
  }

  .legal-back {
    display: inline-block;
    font-size: 15px;
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }

  .legal-title {
    font-size: clamp(40px, 6vw, 56px);
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: -0.04em;
    line-height: 1.05;
  }

  .legal-updated {
    margin-top: 12px;
    font-size: 15px;
    color: var(--text-tertiary);
  }
</style>
